B.Tr=s(["My scientific name is Bubo scandiacus.","Unlike many close relatives, I often hunt during daylight.","Periodic movements far south of my usual range are called irruptions.","Dense feathers cover even my legs and feet.","Lemmings form a major part of my diet in the Arctic.","Females usually carry more dark markings than adult males.","I nest on open tundra rather than in trees.","My eyes are bright yellow and face forward.","My mostly white plumage blends into snow.","Hedwig in the Harry Potter stories is one of my species."],t.s)
B.a_9=new A.aX("animals_birds_0001","Snowy Owl","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/01_snowy_owl.webp",B.Tr,B.N)
B.QU=s(["My scientific name is Alcedo atthis.","I excavate a nesting tunnel in a vertical riverbank.","Much of my blue colour is structural rather than produced by blue pigment.","I may beat a captured fish against a perch before swallowing it.","A clear inner eyelid protects my eyes underwater.","I watch for prey from a low branch above still or slow-moving water.","My flight is fast, low and direct along rivers.","My upperparts look electric blue and my underparts orange.","I plunge head-first into water to catch small fish.","My name combines royalty with a person who catches fish."],t.s)
B.Tz=s(["kingfisher"],t.s)
B.ZW=new A.aX("animals_birds_0002","Common Kingfisher","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/02_common_kingfisher.webp",B.QU,B.Tz)
B.Tb=s(["My scientific name is Phoenicopterus roseus.","Both parents can feed a chick with a nutritious secretion called crop milk.","Comb-like structures called lamellae help my bill filter food from water.","I often feed with my head upside down.","Carotenoids in my diet influence the colour of my feathers.","I live around shallow saline lagoons, mudflats and lakes.","I breed in large, noisy colonies and build a mud mound nest.","My long neck and legs are adapted for wading.","I am famous for sometimes resting on one leg.","My plumage is pale pink and my bill curves downward."],t.s)
B.Tc=s(["flamingo"],t.s)
B.a_5=new A.aX("animals_birds_0003","Greater Flamingo","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/03_greater_flamingo.webp",B.Tb,B.Tc)
B.Sb=s(["My scientific name is Fratercula arctica.","After breeding, colourful outer plates on my bill are shed.","Backward-pointing structures in my mouth help me hold several fish at once.","I spend most of the year far out at sea.","I use my wings to \u2018fly\u2019 underwater while chasing fish.","I nest in a burrow or rock crevice on coastal islands and cliffs.","My range lies across the cold North Atlantic.","My body is black and white, with orange legs in breeding season.","My large triangular bill becomes brightly coloured in spring.","I am sometimes nicknamed the clown or parrot of the sea."],t.s)
B.TR=s(["puffin"],t.s)
B.a_i=new A.aX("animals_birds_0004","Atlantic Puffin","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/04_atlantic_puffin.webp",B.Sb,B.TR)
B.SH=s(["My scientific name is Pavo cristatus.","The spectacular \u2018tail\u2019 displayed by males is mainly made of elongated upper-tail coverts.","A male vibrates these feathers during courtship, creating a subtle rattling sound.","The circular markings on the train are called ocelli.","I naturally occur across the Indian subcontinent but have been introduced elsewhere.","I am the national bird of India.","Males are iridescent blue, while females are mostly brown and green.","The general name for both sexes is peafowl.","A female is called a peahen.","A male is called a peacock and can fan an enormous eye-spotted train."],t.s)
B.S3=s(["Indian Peafowl","Peafowl"],t.s)
B.a_a=new A.aX("animals_birds_0005","Peacock","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/05_indian_peafowl.webp",B.SH,B.S3)
B.QH=s(["My scientific name is Haliaeetus leucocephalus.","My species name refers to a \u2018white-headed sea eagle\u2019 rather than a lack of feathers.","I sometimes steal fish caught by other birds.","My enormous stick nests can be reused and enlarged for many years.","Young birds remain mostly brown for several years.","I am usually found near large rivers, lakes and coasts.","Fish make up much of my diet.","Adults have a dark brown body, white head and white tail.","My hooked bill and feet are bright yellow.","I am the national bird and emblem of the United States."],t.s)
B.a_A=new A.aX("animals_birds_0006","Bald Eagle","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/06_bald_eagle.webp",B.QH,B.N)
B.Rr=s(["My scientific name is Archilochus colubris.","I can enter a low-energy state called torpor to conserve energy overnight.","Many of my kind cross the Gulf of Mexico during migration.","The male\u2019s brilliant throat patch is called a gorget.","My wings rotate at the shoulder in a figure-eight motion.","I can fly backwards as well as hover in place.","I feed on flower nectar but also catch tiny insects.","My long slender bill reaches deep into tubular flowers.","I am a tiny green bird with extremely rapid wingbeats.","The adult male has a shimmering red throat."],t.s)
B.Uw=s(["hummingbird","humming bird","ruby throated hummingbird","ruby throated humming bird"],t.s)
B.a_E=new A.aX("animals_birds_0007","Ruby-throated Hummingbird","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/07_ruby_throated_hummingbird.webp",B.Rr,B.Uw)
B.QV=s(["My scientific name is Ramphastos toco.","Blood flow through my bill helps me release excess body heat.","My feet are zygodactyl, with two toes pointing forward and two backward.","Despite its size, my bill is lightweight because its interior has a foam-like structure.","I nest inside tree cavities.","I eat mainly fruit, although I may also take insects, eggs and small animals.","I am native to South America, especially open woodland and forest edges.","My body is mostly black with a white throat.","My bill is enormous, orange and black-tipped.","I am the largest and probably most recognisable toucan species."],t.s)
B.Ui=s(["toucan"],t.s)
B.a_p=new A.aX("animals_birds_0008","Toco Toucan","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/08_toco_toucan.webp",B.QV,B.Ui)
B.SO=s(["My scientific name is Aptenodytes forsteri.","The male balances a single egg on his feet beneath a brood pouch.","During winter incubation, males may fast for around two months.","Colonies huddle and rotate positions to conserve heat.","I can dive hundreds of metres and remain underwater for more than 20 minutes.","I breed on Antarctic sea ice during the coldest season.","I am the tallest and heaviest living penguin.","Adults have yellow-orange patches on the upper chest and neck.","I cannot fly, but my wings act as powerful flippers underwater.","My name is the highest royal title followed by a black-and-white seabird."],t.s)
B.TQ=s(["penguin"],t.s)
B.a_3=new A.aX("animals_birds_0009","Emperor Penguin","assets/images/categories/animals/birds/09_emperor_penguin.webp",B.SO,B.TQ)
B.Sm=s(["My scientific name is Erithacus rubecula.","Both sexes defend territories and may sing during winter.","Early English speakers called my breast \u2018red\u2019 before the word orange became common.","I often follow gardeners to search freshly turned soil for insects.","Juveniles are speckled brown and lack the adult\u2019s bright breast.","I am common in gardens, woodland and hedgerows across Europe.","I am strongly associated with British Christmas cards.","My song is thin, sweet and slightly wistful.","I am a small brown bird with an orange-red face and breast.","My familiar name is also a common human first name."],t.s)
B.U7=s(["robin"],t.s)
